</div>

        
            












<div class="row-card">
  <div class="row-card__container">
    
    <div class="row-card__body">
        
          <a class="row-card__heading glue-link" href=https://research.google/pubs/%CF%80-flux-tuning-of-quantum-paramagnetism-in-the-triangular-lattice-hubbard-model/ >
            
              π-Flux Tuning of Quantum Paramagnetism in the Triangular-Lattice Hubbard Model
            
          </a>
        
        <div class="row-card__subheading">
          
            
              
                
                  
                    <div class="row-card__subheading__item small-text">
                      
                        Zhaochen Liu
                      
                    </div>
                
              
            
              
                
                  
                    <div class="row-card__subheading__spacer"></div>
                    <div class="row-card__subheading__item small-text">
                      
                        <a class="row-card__small-link" href="/people/andreasfeuerpfeil/">
                          Andreas Feuerpfeil
                        </a>
                      
                    </div>
                  
              
            
              
                
                  
                    <div class="row-card__subheading__spacer"></div>
                    <div class="row-card__subheading__item small-text">
                      
                        Ronny Thomale
                      
                    </div>
                  
              
            
          
          
          <div class="row-card__subheading__spacer"></div>
          <div class="row-card__subheading__item small-text">
             (2026)
          </div>
          
        </div>
    </div>
    
    
    
    <div class="row-card__cta headline-6">
      <div class="glue-tooltip" data-glue-tooltip-auto-position="false">
        















<button class="glue-button glue-button--high-emphasis glue-tooltip__trigger"  aria-describedby=tooltip-contentwe-compare-two-time-reversal-symme tabindex=0 >
  


<span class="js-gt-item-id">Preview</span>




</button>




        <span id="tooltip-contentwe-compare-two-time-reversal-symme" class="glue-tooltip__content" role="tooltip">
          <span data-tooltip-type="simple">
              Preview abstract
          </span>
          <span data-tooltip-type="rich">
              <span class="glue-tooltip__body">We compare two time-reversal-symmetric triangular-lattice Hubbard models at half filling: the zero-flux model and a staggered π-flux model with zero and π flux through oppositely oriented triangles. Although both reduce to the same Heisenberg model at leading order in the strong-coupling limit, their distinct charge fluctuation profiles yield different quantum paramagnetic regimes. Combining a strong-coupling expansion with infinite density matrix renormalization group (iDMRG) calculations, we find that the positive ring-exchange of the zero-flux model promotes spontaneous chirality, consistent with its notion of a chiral spin liquid at intermediate coupling. In the staggered-π-flux model, whose noninteracting limit is a Dirac semimetal, the ring exchange changes sign and disfavors chiral order and we find no resolvable scalar chirality. This renders flux-tuned ring-exchange an efficient discriminator between chiral and non-chiral quantum paramagnets at finite coupling.</span>
              















<a class="glue-button glue-button--high-emphasis" href="https://research.google/pubs/%CF%80-flux-tuning-of-quantum-paramagnetism-in-the-triangular-lattice-hubbard-model/"   >
  


<span class="js-gt-item-id">View details</span>




</a>



          </span>
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
    
    
  </div>
</div>

        
            












